// amount is fictional: the loan was rescaled to a different flat price and the
// derived rows (IP interest, INT-R rebates, BAL-CF balances) were recomputed,
// so the whole thing still reconciles to the cent without publishing anybody
// else's mortgage. The handful of figures that had to stay real — the ones
// proving our formulas match what the bank actually charges — live as
// individual constants in tests/loanstatement.mjs instead.
